    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d12-a5">

                <pb facs="0245" n="235" xml:id="pg235"/>

                <head>Appendix D to HD–96</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">polish
                            delegation<lb/>to the<lb/>peace conference</hi>
                        <lb/> 15 Avenue George V.</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-11-17">November 17, 1919</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#flush">To the Secretary General of the Peace Conference:</p>
                <p>I have the honor to acknowledge receipt of your letter of November 12<anchor
                        n="10" xml:id="d12-f1"/> and to inform you, at the same time, that the
                    Polish Plenipotentiary Delegates, Messrs. Ladislas Grabski and Stanislas Patek
                    have arrived in Paris and are ready to comply with the invitation of the Supreme
                    Council.</p>
                <p>The Polish Delegates would be pleased to become acquainted with the new draft of
                    statute for Eastern Galicia, before they set forth their observations on the
                    said statute.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
